    "evidence_text": "We propose a scaling model that enables the DV pattern to adjust proportionally to embryonic axis size.\n\nIn this paper, we address the role of Notch signalling in vivo during chick myogenesis.\n\nHow is such a morphogenetic field established?\n\nADMP transcription in the Spemann organizer is activated at low BMP levels.\n\nWhen ventral BMP2/4/7 signals are depleted, Admp expression increases, allowing for self-regulation.\n\nADMP has BMP-like activity and signals via the ALK-2 receptor.\n\nIt is unable to signal dorsally because of inhibition by Chordin.\n\nThe ventral BMP antagonists Sizzled and Bambi further refine the pattern.\n\nInhibition of limb regeneration in the axolotl after treatment of the skin with actinomycin D.\n\nAfter an initial healing period, the control limbs regenerated normally.\n\nThe Spemann Organizer Signal noggin Binds and Inactivates Bone Morphogenetic Protein 4\n\nThese data suggest that noggin secreted by the organizer patterns the embryo by interrupting BMP signaling.\n\nRegulation of Pax-3 expression in the dermomyotome and its role in muscle development.\n\nEmerging mechanisms in morphogen-mediated axon guidance.",
